::ENG4_U03_L06_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.R.12] Text A: The city should add crosswalk lights near the senior center because traffic reports show three near-miss incidents this year. Text B: Our seniors should not have to gamble with traffic just to reach the grocery store. Which comparison best evaluates the rhetorical choices?
{
~A. Text A is emotional, while Text B avoids emotion completely.#Incorrect
~B. Text B is ineffective because it does not include a statistic.#Incorrect
=C. Text A uses documented evidence for practical credibility, while Text B uses vivid language to create urgency.#Correct
~D. Both texts use identical rhetorical strategies because they support the same safety goal.#Incorrect
}
::ENG4_U03_L06_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.V.03] Passage: "The proposal is not a burden; it is an investment in student access." Which word relationship most shapes the tone?
{
=B. The contrast between "burden" and "investment" reframes the proposal positively.#Correct
~A. The phrase "student access" creates a humorous tone.#Incorrect
~C. The word "proposal" creates a hostile tone.#Incorrect
~D. The sentence avoids any rhetorical choice.#Incorrect
}
::ENG4_U03_L06_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.R.07] Passage: A workplace memo begins with accident statistics before recommending required safety training. What purpose most likely explains this opening?
{
~C. To distract readers from the recommendation.#Incorrect
~B. To make the issue seem less serious.#Incorrect
=A. To establish that the recommendation responds to a documented problem.#Correct
~D. To replace the need for a claim.#Incorrect
}
::ENG4_U03_L06_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.R.08] Text A supports a policy with cost data. Text B supports the same policy with a personal story. Which evaluation is most precise?
{
~A. Text A is always stronger because data are always objective.#Incorrect
~B. Text B is always stronger because stories are easier to remember.#Incorrect
~C. Both texts are weak because they use different kinds of evidence.#Incorrect
=D. Text A may be stronger for decision-makers, while Text B may be stronger for a public audience needing emotional connection.#Correct
}
::ENG4_U03_L06_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.R.12] Text A: "The pilot program reduced wait times by 18 percent." Text B: "No patient should spend an afternoon wondering whether help will arrive." Which rhetorical choice does Text B use most clearly?
{
~A. Technical terminology to establish professional expertise.#Incorrect
=B. Emotional appeal through direct, human-centered language.#Correct
~C. Statistical comparison to prove the program's efficiency.#Incorrect
~D. Chronological organization to show a sequence of events.#Incorrect
}
